      "side": 1,
      "message": "hi @ffilzlnx@mindspring.com,\nPrometheus variables are typically declared as Counter, Gauge, or Histogram. While Prometheus does not support string formats directly, we can define strings within labels, as shown below:\n\nganesha_version{GANESHA_VERSION\u003d\"7-dev.7\"} 0\n\nSince using a value of 0 would be meaningless, I propose that we set the value of this metric to GANESHA_MAJOR_NUMBER instead, so that the full version information is available within the labels.\n\n\nAlso @yonic@google.com,\nWould it be appropriate to use the monitoring__register_gauge() function to register the Ganesha version metric, rather than using the \"initializer list\" style?",
      "revId": "90cd3d3000f63dc62f7c36be99a9cb6fec50f519",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
